From 8503ae45871cbe0aaac672f1dd0ba139ff6c3e64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 19:55:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: show a fight's consensus on whichever market the drawer
 opened
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The consensus attaches to the moneyline, because that is the only market
with a fighter side for it to be with or against. But Full Slate's "More
info" opens openStatsDrawer on bestCandidateForGame() — the best-scoring
candidate across h2h, spreads and totals — and for MMA that is routinely the
rounds total. So the section rendered as nothing on exactly the drawer people
open, which reads as the feed not arriving at all.

The drawer now falls back to the fight's own feed entry when the leg it
opened on has no swing of its own. `scored` carries whether the swing
actually moved THIS pick's grade, so a totals drawer says the consensus is
context for the fight rather than claiming it changed a grade it never
touched. Scoring is unchanged: still moneyline-only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ko7MvVdXhjZNR67gyhzZq3
